sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a periodic 22.42 µm detail patch for Holocene Coturnix japonica. Linear k_c^2 = 3112/259, sigma_max = 0.513 at the nominal point, equal-diffusion sigma_max = -0.070. A five-point Du sweep of the early-time growth wavelength tracks the linear law with Pearson r = 0.9997 and RMSE = 6.52 µm (the growth moment sits long of k_c). The saturated display spacing is 33.6 µm. The Yehliu CC BY-SA portrait is segmented and used as the envelope for a 12-frame 960×540 growth GIF. Computer-vision similarity of the last frame to the photograph is 96.0. Ablation activator std is 0.0003 against a patterned std of 1.04. Overall 86.2/100. The growth-moment bias, the saturated-versus-linear gap, and the single plumage ROI are the remediation targets. Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 85.4, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 624782 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 1c2ebe1960b77d716273802266e563ebb8e7ac52ed4b8869d4a84a97de8367f7 (sha256 1c2ebe1960b77d716273802266e563ebb8e7ac52ed4b8869d4a84a97de8367f7), spec_fingerprint fcce03b3209888bbee04f33bf08d93db2245049fdd963bb6413cf49a32f9a400. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fcce03b3209888bbee04f33bf08d93db2245049fdd963bb6413cf49a32f9a400; artifact_sha256: 1c2ebe1960b77d716273802266e563ebb8e7ac52ed4b8869d4a84a97de8367f7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/coturnix_japonica_yehliu_taiwan.jpg=e3ba62e08042fc74..., datasets/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=1f2c15cdb72b9ad0...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Prum & Williamson 2002: within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as follicular reaction-diffusion. | Harris et al. 2005: Shh self-activates and induces Bmp2; Bmp2 represses Shh on the feather epithelium. | Haupaix et al. 2018 and Inaba & Chuong 2020: Japanese quail has a somite-scale macro pattern and a within-feather micro pattern.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters (a, b, Du, Dv) = (0.07, 0.93, 0.035, 1.85) with the length unit fixed so lambda_c = 2.242e-5 m. | A Du sweep of the linear-regime growth wavelength, an equal-diffusion ablation, and a mildly anisotropic display field. | Plumage-mask segmentation of the Yehliu photograph and a high-frequency composite of the micro-mode onto that Holocene envelope.; transfer_boundary: The Yehliu portrait has no micron scale bar. Pixel wavelength in the GIF is a display convention. The 22.42 µm figure is the linear law, not a photogrammetric length. | Saturated spot spacing on the display grid is about 33.6 µm, longer than the linear 22.42 µm. Those are different measurements.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Schnakenberg rates are fitted Shh/Bmp2 biochemical constants. | Does not claim a geological shift from a named fossil chronospecies. The series is one Holocene node at 0 Ma. | Does not claim the somite-stripe script (beta_A = 0.22, d = 20) was reused.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'The linear-regime wavelength is a power-weighted first moment and sits ~6.5 µm long of k_c. Replace it with a parabolic fit to the growth peak and recompute Pearson r and RMSE.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Report saturated display spacing and linear lambda as separate annotated lengths on the comparison figure so 33.6 µm is not read as the slot wavelength.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Add a second plumage ROI (flank-only, straw excluded) and repeat the melanin-fraction and coherency measurements so the single mask is not the only specimen number.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'No independent second assessor is available in this single-agent loop. Leave the score as builder-assessed; do not invent a second signature.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.862"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent round; second assessor not available)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

